
# Contributing Guidelines

Thank you for your interest in contributing to our application suite! Because our software architecture relies on a structured, centralized framework (including our Flutter frontends and serverless AWS backend), contributions are managed carefully to maintain security, stability, and performance.

## How to Contribute
While our core application suite and proprietary source code are managed internally, we welcome feedback, bug reports, and feature suggestions.

### Reporting Bugs and Issues
If you encounter a bug or unexpected behavior in any of our applications (including our chat utilities like Nucy):
1. Check the existing issues or closed feedback logs to see if it has already been reported.
2. Open a new issue with a clear, descriptive title.
3. Provide steps to reproduce the issue, device/OS details, and screenshots or logs if applicable.

### Suggesting Enhancements
We are always looking to improve our utility fleet and agentic features. When suggesting a new feature:
* Explain clearly what the feature should do.
* Describe why this feature would be useful for the broader user base.
* Provide examples or use cases if possible.

